1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,813
This town loses gravity for one minute every day.

2
00:00:02,893 --> 00:00:04,580
At exactly twelve o'clock.

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:05,947
A siren goes off,

4
00:00:06,027 --> 00:00:07,880
and everyone grabs the nearest railing.

5
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,313
Because if you don't... you float.

6
00:00:10,393 --> 00:00:11,647
Cars float.

7
00:00:11,727 --> 00:00:13,047
Dogs float.

8
00:00:13,127 --> 00:00:15,280
Even the mayor's toupee floats.

9
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,513
Sixty seconds later, everything drops.

10
00:00:17,593 --> 00:00:20,147
We call it Float Hour. Even though it's a minute.

11
00:00:20,227 --> 00:00:21,169
I'm Ryan.

12
00:00:21,327 --> 00:00:22,813
This is my little brother, Bo.

13
00:00:22,893 --> 00:00:24,880
Bo has never held a railing in his life.

14
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,113
He says floating is the best part of the day.

15
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:30,613
Our grandpa Gus winds the giant town clock every morning.

16
00:00:30,693 --> 00:00:32,047
He told us one rule.

17
00:00:32,127 --> 00:00:33,613
"If the clock ever stops...

18
00:00:33,693 --> 00:00:35,759
hold on, and don't let go."

19
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:36,980
Bo laughed.

20
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:38,347
Then came Tuesday.

21
00:00:38,427 --> 00:00:40,590
11:59. The siren.

22
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,213
Everyone grabbed a railing.

23
00:00:42,293 --> 00:00:43,847
Bo grabbed his balloon.

24
00:00:43,927 --> 00:00:45,745
Twelve o'clock. We floated.

25
00:00:45,927 --> 00:00:48,097
Ten seconds. Thirty. Sixty.

26
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:49,513
Nothing came down.

27
00:00:49,593 --> 00:00:50,780
The clock had stopped.

28
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:52,247
And everything kept going up.

29
00:00:52,327 --> 00:00:55,101
Cars. Mailboxes. The school bus.

30
00:00:55,227 --> 00:00:57,747
The fountain water floated up in giant bubbles.

31
00:00:57,827 --> 00:01:00,098
Bo waved at me... and kept rising.

32
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:01,647
I screamed his name.

33
00:01:01,727 --> 00:01:04,913
Grandpa yelled, "The key! Someone stole the key!"

34
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:07,147
Without the key, the clock can't be wound.

35
00:01:07,227 --> 00:01:09,747
And without the clock, there's no gravity at all.

36
00:01:09,827 --> 00:01:12,413
The whole town was drifting into the clouds.

37
00:01:12,493 --> 00:01:13,647
That's when I saw him.

38
00:01:13,727 --> 00:01:15,853
Mayor Grimsby. Holding the key.

39
00:01:16,027 --> 00:01:17,980
"No more Float Hour," he said.

40
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:20,413
"From now on... it's Float Forever!"

41
00:01:20,493 --> 00:01:22,580
His new sky hotel opens tomorrow.

42
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:23,747
So I let go.

43
00:01:23,827 --> 00:01:26,313
I pushed off a lamppost and flew straight at him.

44
00:01:26,393 --> 00:01:27,780
Biscuit flew with me.

45
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,313
Biscuit bit the toupee.

46
00:01:29,393 --> 00:01:30,780
The mayor dropped the key.

47
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:31,697
I caught it.

48
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,468
Gravity: three percent.

49
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:35,647
I grabbed Bo's shoelace on the way up.

50
00:01:35,727 --> 00:01:37,580
Grandpa held the clock door open.

51
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,313
The keyhole was taller than me.

52
00:01:39,393 --> 00:01:42,780
We all pushed. Once. Twice. Three times.

53
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:44,613
The gears roared back to life.

54
00:01:44,693 --> 00:01:45,163
Tick.

55
00:01:45,993 --> 00:01:48,488
Everything came down. Really fast.

56
00:01:48,627 --> 00:01:50,247
The mayor landed in the fountain.

57
00:01:50,327 --> 00:01:52,047
His toupee landed on Biscuit.

58
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:53,880
Biscuit refuses to give it back.

59
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:56,113
Now the key hangs around Grandpa's neck.

60
00:01:56,193 --> 00:01:58,564
The mayor? He polishes railings now.

61
00:01:58,693 --> 00:02:00,955
And Bo holds a railing. Mostly.

62
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,513
Everything was normal again.

63
00:02:02,593 --> 00:02:04,713
But last night, I woke up at 3 a.m.

64
00:02:04,793 --> 00:02:06,447
My bed was touching the ceiling.

65
00:02:06,527 --> 00:02:08,413
And the clock tower said twelve o'clock.

66
00:02:08,493 --> 00:02:09,880
Someone else has a key.

67
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:10,830
Hold on.

